{# What the incoming category shows while its results are still being fetched.

   Reached only when the swipe's neighbour cache misses — a search or a mutation
   since the neighbours were primed, or a gesture begun before the prime landed.
   The common case never renders this at all.

   It is a designed state rather than a failure: the gesture still follows the
   thumb at its usual rate, and this is what occupies the incoming panel until
   the grid arrives to replace it. Deliberately just the app's spinner, with no
   wording — the panel is on screen for a fraction of a second on a local server,
   and a sentence nobody can finish reading is worse than a mark that says only
   "working".

   Lives in a <template> so gallery.js clones markup rather than assembling HTML
   in a string; the gesture has no business knowing what a spinner looks like.

   aria-hidden: the incoming panel is mid-gesture and not yet the view. What the
   viewer is told about the new category is announced when it becomes the active
   one, by the same title change every other category switch makes. #}
<div class="swipe-placeholder" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="spinner"></div>
</div>
